From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:43:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Store redstone signal suppression on world tick threads

Provide a per-world-tick-thread wire signal flag so parallel world redstone queries avoid ThreadLocal lookups. The Minecraft wire patch retains a fallback for other threads and restores prior state.

diff --git a/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/common/util/TickThread.java b/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/common/util/TickThread.java
index a3690445efe304e1ba26cf9e9b9fb10b9e8a82d0..a5c27da1fa1e94dbc968829058a1ffa765861da3 100644
--- a/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/common/util/TickThread.java
+++ b/src/main/java/ca/spottedleaf/moonrise/common/util/TickThread.java
@@ -259,6 +259,7 @@ public class TickThread extends Thread {
     public static class ServerLevelTickThread extends TickThread {
 
         public net.minecraft.server.level.ServerLevel currentTickingServerLevel;
+        public boolean redstoneWireShouldSignal = true;
 
         public ServerLevelTickThread(final String name) {
             super(name);
